<%# One row of the User view — the dashboard's decision board.

    The whole premise of this screen is that a decision can be taken ON the row.
    So everything the decision turns on is inline: what the session is, where it
    stands in its own words, whether its PR is green, and the three buttons that
    act on it (Merge, Snooze, Trash). Nothing here opens a session to find out
    anything.

    Layout is mobile-first and single-column inside the row: a flex-wrapping
    header line, the generated status blurb, then a flex-wrapping action line.
    Wrapping rather than a grid is what keeps it inside 375px without any of the
    buttons sliding off the right edge — every child is `shrink-0` except the
    title, which is the one thing allowed to take the remaining width.

    Locals:
      agent_session - the session %>
<%
  pr = Sessions::PrSummary.for(agent_session)
  priority_class = agent_session.priority_class(cached_genesis_overrides)
  is_priority = priority_class == SessionGenesis::PRIORITY
  summary = agent_session.status_summary
  line_count = agent_session.transcript_line_count
  behind = summary&.messages_since(line_count).to_i
%>
<%# `data-visibility-unit` is what lets the shared visibility controller take this
    row off the board when Snooze or Hide succeeds, with no reload. `data-precedence`
    and `data-priority-class` are what the user-view controller re-sorts on after a
    drag or a restore. %>
<li id="<%= user_view_row_dom_id(agent_session) %>"
    class="flex items-start gap-2 px-3 py-3 sm:gap-3"
    data-visibility-unit
    data-user-view-target="row"
    data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
    data-precedence="<%= agent_session.precedence %>"
    data-priority-class="<%= priority_class %>">

  <%# Drag handle. Padded into a touch target rather than sized as one — SortableJS
      only starts a drag from inside this box, and a 16px one on a phone is a box
      you miss. %>
  <span class="shrink-0 cursor-grab px-1 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:text-gray-500"
        data-user-view-target="handle" aria-hidden="true" title="Drag to reorder">
    <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M7 4a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zM7 9a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm-6 5a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2z"/></svg>
  </span>

  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <%# ---- Identity line: title, class, status ---- %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
      <%# A real <a href> whose plain left-click opens the right-side drawer rather
          than navigating off the board — the same interception the Ranked view's
          title uses, and for the same reason: losing your place on a list you are
          working top to bottom is the one thing this screen must not do. %>
      <%= link_to agent_session.title.presence || "Untitled session",
            session_path(agent_session),
            data: session_drawer_link_data(agent_session, turbo_prefetch: false),
            class: "min-w-0 flex-1 basis-full break-words text-sm font-medium text-gray-800 hover:text-indigo-600 sm:basis-auto sm:truncate" %>

      <%# The priority/spot affordance. The list is not split into two sections, so
          this badge is the only thing that says which half of the ordering a row
          is in — and why a spot row can never be dragged above a priority one. %>
      <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-medium <%= is_priority ? "bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700" : "bg-amber-100 text-amber-700" %>"
            title="<%= is_priority ? "Priority — starts whenever it is ready. Priority rows sort above every spot row." : "Spot — starts when there is quota room, highest precedence first." %>">
        <%= is_priority ? "Priority" : "Spot" %>
      </span>

      <span class="shrink-0"><%= render "sessions/status_badge", agent_session: agent_session %></span>

      <% unless agent_session.board_visible? %>
        <span class="shrink-0"><%= render "sessions/visibility_badge", agent_session: agent_session %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# ---- The generated status ----

        Zimmer's own cached "where this stands" blurb (SessionStatusSummary),
        written by an agent when the session comes to rest. Clamped to three lines
        with the full text on hover, and marked stale by message count rather than
        by age — a summary does not rot because time passed, it rots because the
        session said something new. Read straight off the eager-loaded association,
        so a hundred rows cost one extra query rather than a hundred.

        Rendered as inline markdown, so its links are clickable — and only inline:
        a paragraph break or a code block would push the row's layout around. The
        text is the stored one rather than `summary_markdown`, whose `#message-N`
        fragments only mean something on the session's own page. A link here is
        never a drag: SortableJS starts one only from the handle. %>
    <% if summary&.summary.present? %>
      <p class="mt-1 line-clamp-3 break-words text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 [&_a]:text-indigo-600 [&_a]:underline [&_a:hover]:text-indigo-800 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-gray-100 [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-gray-700"
         title="<%= markdown_plain_text(summary.summary) %>"><%= inline_markdown(summary.summary) %></p>

      <%# Freshness, on every row rather than only the stale ones, so a row with no
          chip never has to be read as "probably fine". Same count the Status panel
          uses; the chip is the at-a-glance half and the words beside it say by how
          much. As of page load: nothing re-renders a row when its summary lands —
          SessionStatusSummary broadcasts only the Status panel. %>
      <% freshness = status_summary_freshness(summary, line_count) %>
      <p class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1.5 gap-y-0.5 text-[11px] text-gray-400"
         data-summary-freshness="<%= freshness %>">
        <% case freshness %>
        <% when :regenerating %>
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-indigo-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-medium text-indigo-700"
                title="A new summary was being written when this page loaded. Reload to see it once it lands.">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 animate-pulse motion-reduce:animate-none rounded-full bg-indigo-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>Regenerating
          </span>
        <% when :stale %>
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-amber-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-medium text-amber-700"
                title="The session has moved since this was written, so it describes an earlier point.">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>Stale
          </span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-medium text-emerald-700"
                title="No messages have landed in the session since this was written.">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>Up to date
          </span>
        <% end %>
        <% if behind.positive? %>
          <span class="min-w-0"><%= pluralize(behind, "message") %> since this was written</span>
        <% end %>
        <% if summary.generated_at %>
          <span class="min-w-0" title="<%= summary.generated_at.utc.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC") %>">written <%= time_ago_in_words(summary.generated_at) %> ago</span>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs italic text-gray-400">No status summary yet.</p>
    <% end %>

    <%# ---- Action line ---- %>
    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <span class="shrink-0 max-w-full truncate rounded bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-gray-500"
            title="Agent root"><%= agent_session.agent_root_key.presence || agent_session.genesis_key %></span>

      <%# The live precedence readout. The user-view controller rewrites it in place
          after a drag, so the number never disagrees with where the row is sitting. %>
      <span class="shrink-0 tabular-nums text-[11px] text-gray-400"
            data-user-view-precedence
            title="Precedence — higher is worked sooner">#<%= agent_session.precedence %></span>

      <%# The PR button, with its green / merged affordance: the glyph's shape and
          colour carry the lifecycle state and the dot beside it carries CI. %>
      <span class="shrink-0"><%= render "sessions/github_pr_link", agent_session: agent_session %></span>

      <%= render "sessions/user_view_merge_button", agent_session: agent_session %>

      <%# Snooze. Presentation only — it takes the row off the board and changes
          nothing about when the session runs. The wrapper is `relative` because the
          popover positions against it. %>
      <span class="relative shrink-0">
        <%= render "sessions/visibility_menu", agent_session: agent_session, variant: :button, compact: true %>
      </span>

      <%# Trash. Posts to the same #archive action every other Trash affordance in
          the app posts to, so the queued-message speed bump and the Undo toast come
          with it — and the row leaves over the turbo stream that action already
          answers with, rather than being taken away optimistically on click. That
          matters here: the first click over a non-empty queue does NOT archive, and
          a row the browser had already removed would claim otherwise. %>
      <%= button_to archive_session_path(agent_session),
            method: :post,
            form: { data: { turbo: true }, class: "shrink-0" },
            class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-red-200 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-red-600 hover:bg-red-50 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-1 focus:ring-red-500",
            title: "Move session #{agent_session.id} to trash" do %>
        <svg class="-ml-0.5 mr-1.5 h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M9 2a1 1 0 00-.894.553L7.382 4H4a1 1 0 000 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h8a2 2 0 002-2V6a1 1 0 100-2h-3.382l-.724-1.447A1 1 0 0011 2H9zM7 8a1 1 0 012 0v6a1 1 0 11-2 0V8zm5-1a1 1 0 00-1 1v6a1 1 0 102 0V8a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
        </svg>
        Trash
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</li>
